{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_35","type":"agent_message","text":"I found another limit in the material binding: `material_clean` checks tracked files only at the start and end. The reflog witness catches commit movement, but misses an uncommitted fix applied while a check runs and then restored with `git restore`. That can leave a passing result eligible for carry even though it was observed against different code. I’m checking how this affects the spec’s D1 safety claim.\n"}}
