{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_43","type":"agent_message","text":"The new finding has a concrete source-derived sequence: start clean, temporarily apply an uncommitted fix, let the affected check pass, then restore the file before final cleanliness checks. HEAD, its reflog length, and endpoint status all match. The next carry can reuse that pass. The review therefore requests a stable execution snapshot or an equivalent guarantee, with a regression covering this sequence.\n"}}
