{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_48","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"git status --porcelain=v1; git diff --check; nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go | sed -n '1619,1636p'; nl -ba .pose/specs/2026-11-22-pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks.md | sed -n '250,254p'\"","aggregated_output":"  1619\tfunc validationSummaryOf(run validationRunResult) *validationSummary {\n  1620\t\tsummary := &validationSummary{Outcome: run.Outcome}\n  1621\t\tfor _, check := range run.Checks {\n  1622\t\t\tcommand := strings.TrimSpace(check.Program + \" \" + strings.Join(check.Args, \" \"))\n  1623\t\t\tif check.Outcome != \"skipped\" && command != \"\" {\n  1624\t\t\t\tsummary.Commands = append(summary.Commands, command)\n  1625\t\t\t}\n  1626\t\t\tline := \"- [\" + check.Outcome + \"] \" + check.ID\n  1627\t\t\tswitch {\n  1628\t\t\tcase check.SkipReason != \"\":\n  1629\t\t\t\tline += \" (\" + check.SkipReason + \")\"\n  1630\t\t\tcase check.DurationSeconds > 0:\n  1631\t\t\t\tline += fmt.Sprintf(\" (%.1fs)\", check.DurationSeconds)\n  1632\t\t\t}\n  1633\t\t\tif check.ExitCode != nil {\n  1634\t\t\t\tline += fmt.Sprintf(\" exit=%d\", *check.ExitCode)\n  1635\t\t\t}\n  1636\t\t\tsummary.Results = append(summary.Results, line)\n   250\tAn instance that declares a module self-contained while its checks read files outside it would carry a stale result. The declaration is explicit and documented, and the default stays the full fallback.\n   251\t\n   252\t### Follow-ups\n   253\t- [open] F1: cover with an end-to-end test that a review bundle sealed over a carried record judges the carried head (seal, verify and closeout-check on a fixture). (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-12-15)\n   254\t- [open] F2: `--carry --report` lists carried checks as executed commands without their `carried_from` head and time; exclude them from the executed summary and label reused results (review round 13, N39). (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-12-15)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_49","type":"agent_message","text":"decision: changes-requested\n\nPrior submodule-movement and cancellation blockers are fixed. The three prior report findings remain the existing F2 follow-up.\n\n- **High — N50:** [validate_carry.go:215](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-3255575225/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go:215) reloads mutable module metadata after verifying it against HEAD. Removing a dependency between verification and selection can incorrectly carry an affected module. Final cleanliness permits that metadata edit. Use one verified metadata snapshot throughout planning.\n- **Low — N51:** [validate.go:1623](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-3255575225/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go:1623) still presents carried checks as executed commands in `--report`. This is owned follow-up F2.\n\nBoth strict validation runs passed: **236/236 repository checks** and **233/233 module checks**. Focused tests, focused race tests, delivery-reader tests, and vet also passed. N50 is established by source tracing; scratch creation was denied, preventing a new fixture reproduction.\n\nApplied the review workflow and Go, security, documentation, delivery-evidence, and knowledge rules. No repository changes or attestation were made.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"prior_findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R12-N39\",\n      \"status\": \"not-fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"validate.go:1619-1636 still includes carried commands and omits carried_from/carried_generated_at from report results. Existing spec follow-up F2 at line 254; represented here by N51.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R13-N42\",\n      \"status\": \"not-fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"validate.go:1623-1631 still renders reused commands, outcomes and durations without origin. Existing spec follow-up F2; represented here by N51.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R14-N43\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"validate_carry.go:723-750 witnesses HEAD and every checked-out submodule's reflog. validate.go:1046 and 1449-1450 compare witnesses. TestValidateSubmoduleMovingAndReturningIsNotClean passed in the focused CLI run and focused race run.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R14-N45\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"validate.go:1463-1468 observes runCtx cancellation independently of executed checks. finalizeCancellation at validate_carry.go:698 clears cleanliness and bindings, and planCarry rejects run-level cancellation. TestCarryRefusesABaseCancelledAtRunLevel and TestCancellationMakesBindingsUnavailable passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R14-N44\",\n      \"status\": \"not-fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"validate.go:1623-1636 still lacks carry provenance in the report projection. Existing spec follow-up F2; represented here by N51.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N50\",\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go\",\n      \"line\": 215,\n      \"summary\": \"The pinned module-metadata check is separated from the metadata actually used for selection. Line 131 verifies working bytes against HEAD, line 134 rereads them, and computeChangedScope at line 215 rereads them again at validate_scope.go:129. With committed metadata declaring b dependsOn a, a concurrent edit removing that dependency after verification but before selection makes an a-only change carry b incorrectly. The edit need not be restored: module-metadata.json is administrative under material_binding.go:29-48, so final validationMaterialClean permits it. This violates R2's pinned selection-policy requirement and D1's safety premise. Source-established; no new scratch reproduction was possible.\",\n      \"action\": \"Capture and verify module metadata once, then use that immutable snapshot for every eligibility and selection decision. Add a synchronized regression that changes working metadata between verification and selection and proves that b is selected or carry is refused.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N51\",\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"disposition\": \"follow-up\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go\",\n      \"line\": 1623,\n      \"summary\": \"validationSummaryOf adds carried checks to executed Commands and displays their prior outcome and duration without their original head or time. A newly dated --carry --report therefore misrepresents reused observations as commands executed by this run. This is existing spec follow-up F2.\",\n      \"action\": \"Complete F2: exclude carried checks from executed Commands and label reused results with carried_from and carried_generated_at.\",\n      \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\",\n      \"review_by\": \"2026-12-15\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"sweep\": \"Reviewed the sealed subject against R1-R10, D1-D3, its ADR and prerequisite material-binding ADR. Swept flag compatibility, base eligibility, engine identity, administrative exclusions, renames and unusual names, gitlinks and nested submodules, symlinks and physical aliases, case handling, manifest-free overrides, nested ownership, stack/check changes, dependency and criticality widening, chained carries, cancellation, material bindings, delivery parsing, concurrent canonical publication, help, localized manuals and scaffolds. Focused CLI tests and race tests, delivery-reader tests, vet, artifact-check and both strict validation commands passed. The prerequisite ADR explicitly accepts transient changes-and-restoration of material; that inherited risk is not reported as a new blocker. N50 concerns a separate mutable selection-policy reread that requires no restoration. State-writing assessments were not run because scratch creation failed on the read-only filesystem. Final git status and diff checks were clean.\",\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assumption-integrity\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N50\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Examined explicit selfContained declarations and inherited material-binding limits. Transient material writers are an accepted prerequisite-ADR risk, with immutable execution tracked separately. The new promise that selection uses pinned metadata is not established because planning rereads mutable bytes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-concurrency\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N50\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Cancellation and submodule movement regressions pass, as do focused race tests. Canonical publication retains its write guard and atomic publisher. Concurrent metadata updates can nevertheless narrow selection after verification.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-contracts\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected additive result fields, legacy-record parsing, CLI refusals and the delivery reader. Existing records retain their interpretation; bases lacking new eligibility fields rerun.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-input-errors\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Focused tests exercised incompatible flags, malformed metadata, unsafe revisions, missing results, duplicate IDs, aliases and fallback reasons. Errors remain actionable.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Traced carried_from and carried_generated_at through ParseDeliveryValidationRun. The direct reader regression passed, and both strict matrices passed. The complete carry-to-seal journey remains explicitly tracked as spec follow-up F1.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-observability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N51\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Canonical JSON retains carry provenance and fallback reasons, but the generated report loses that provenance.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"compatibility\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Examined CLI help, argument combinations, schema additions and legacy delivery parsing. The new flag is opt-in and older results remain readable while unsuitable carry bases trigger full execution.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"correctness\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N50\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Existing regression suites and both matrices pass, but the verified metadata and selection metadata can differ, producing an unsound carried result.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"design-causality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N50\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Whole-matrix and engine comparisons implement D2, while declared ownership implements D3. D1 additionally requires selection from the verified policy; rereading working metadata breaks that causal link.\",\n      \"mappings\": [\n        {\n          \"delta\": \"SD-253b523c\",\n          \"basis\": \"D1\",\n          \"disposition\": \"mapped\",\n          \"rationale\": \"The added ADR records the decision to preserve each carried observation's origin while binding the new run to current material, conditional on sound changed-scope selection.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"documentation\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N51\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Compared English and Portuguese manuals, help and scaffold changes against runtime. Carry documentation agrees with the implemented rules, but --report still contradicts its executed-command description.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"operability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N51\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Eligibility refusals and selection explanations are actionable. Report users cannot distinguish carried observations from newly executed commands.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"requirements\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N50\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Reviewed R1-R10 and their fixtures. The metadata equality guard covers pre-existing working edits but does not ensure that R2's pinned policy is the policy R3 selection actually consumes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scope\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-97948d92f0ce316e\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Compared the implementation, delivery reader, help, manuals and ADR with declared artifacts. Changes remain within the approved carry and changed-scope work. Artifact-check exited successfully; its later index-only trailer head is distinct from the sealed semantic subject.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"security\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N50\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Revision confinement and conservative alias refusals are present. Mutable metadata can still cross the verified-policy boundary and authorize stale carry evidence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"solution-proportionality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N50\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Module-level reuse with whole-matrix and engine equality avoids speculative per-check caching. The smallest sufficient correction for N50 is to reuse one verified metadata snapshot throughout planning. A full immutable execution snapshot remains a separately accepted prerequisite follow-up.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"artifact-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks --strict\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Executed and exited 0. Reported provenance warnings, 15 claims and 20 observations, without blocking errors. Its resolved head was the later index-only trailer commit identified in the brief.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-design\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-97948d92f0ce316e\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Executed the requested JSON assessment successfully; its input digest matches the sealed design evidence and it reports SD-253b523c.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-discover\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:mktemp -d /tmp/pose-review-assess.XXXXXX\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Scratch creation failed with Read-only file system. Did not run a state-writing assessment in the sealed checkout.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-integrate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected sealed integration evidence and independently ran both strict matrices. The state-writing assessor was not invoked because a safe scratch copy could not be created.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:mktemp -d /tmp/pose-review-assess.XXXXXX\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The state-writing assessment requires scratch, whose creation was denied. Manually searched the new carry and delivery-reader files for debt markers; no new TODO, FIXME, stub or panic marker was found.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"closeout-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose closeout-check spec:pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Not executed: completion-only verification follows the recorded review conclusion. This request explicitly forbids recording an attestation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"review-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose review-check spec:pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Not executed: it cannot verify this conclusion before POSE records it, and the reviewer was instructed not to record an attestation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"suggest-review\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Executed successfully and applied its Go, security and documentation rule selection.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Independently executed pose validate --strict: exit 0, 236 checks passed. The sealed matrix also supplies build, integration and e2e evidence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Independently executed pose validate --strict --module pose-mcp: exit 0, 233 checks passed. Focused CLI tests, focused race tests, delivery-reader tests and go vet ./internal/cli ./internal/pose also passed.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"}}
